{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/325896-token-shovel-of-death","id":325896,"title":"Token: Shovel of Death","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-30T03:04:01-08:00","id":325896,"title":"Token: Shovel of Death","content":"So one of mine players want to play Gravewight Darkling and wanted to have Token Shovel as he is gravedigger for his Keeper. We have a problem on pricing the item. He want's to make it usable as normal weapon - so I think this would be something like 1 dot power, right? But there we have two ideas. One, the Shovel would let you control the ghosts. Or that Shovel would let you hurt any ephemeral beings - ghosts, spirits, angels, probably Hedge Beast, etc. What would be pricing for this two scenarios on Merits dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T10:26:56-08:00","id":339199,"title":"","content":"If you want to use a shovel as a weapon as-is, I'd say just go with improvised weapon rules. For something a bit more formalized, Rites of Spring has a section on Hedgespun Tokens, including designing your own weapons. Being able to harm ephemeral beings is (and this is just my intuition after skimming through some Tokens) either two or three dots. Two dots for one type of being, three for any kind. Alternatively, two dots to harm any kind of ephemeral being if the drawback is on the nasty side of things. I'm uncertain what you mean by controlling ghosts, but my first guess would be four dots at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T01:16:27-08:00","id":339828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/325896-token-shovel-of-death?p=339199#post339199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, two dots to harm any kind of ephemeral being if the drawback is on the nasty side of things. I'm uncertain what you mean by controlling ghosts, but my first guess would be four dots at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a <b>Mage</b> spell Control Ghost from Death 3. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Isn't there general rule that using <b>Mage</b> spells as items powers will make an Item a Spell Level+1 Merit dots? So this kind of Shovel would make it up to Token 4 dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T08:55:19-08:00","id":340073,"title":"","content":"Hmm, that is true. That's probably a decent starting guideline, though nota bene that Mage and Changeling have different underlying assumptions about power. The Lost should have an undercurrent of powerlessness, I think. Or at the very least, power needs to be won a bit harder--hence questing and all that jazz. So, a four-dot Token that imitates Control Ghost should probably not be a word-for-word copy of the spell, either leaving some feature out or having a bit of an unpleasant drawback (incidentally, I've found that designing decent drawbacks the most difficult part of making Tokens).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}